course: dictionary
lesson: 12151
title: Making things fair again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When something is lost, broken or harmed, or someone works extra hard, it can be fair to give something back. That is what compensated means: someone was given money or something else to make up for it. «The airline compensated the family for their lost bags.» The family lost their bags, so the airline gave them something back. Check it by swapping in made up for: the airline made up for the lost bags.
explain: Look at the words around compensated for clues. Loss, harm, extra hours and flood are clues that a fair payment or reward is coming. «Dad worked extra hours, so he was compensated with a day off.» Extra hours are the clue, and a day off is what he was given in return.
explain: Compensated can also mean one thing balanced or made up for another. «Her strong arms compensated for her short legs in the race.» Her strong arms did not make her legs longer, but they made up for them, so she still ran well. When you see compensated for, ask: what was made up for?
fact: Compensated means given money or something else to make up for a loss, harm or work.
fact: «Compensated for» means made up for, as in «The sunshine compensated for the cold wind.»
fact: Compensate is the verb; compensates, compensating and compensated show when it happens.
fact: Compensation can be money, a day off or a treat, anything given to make things fair again.
fact: Something can also compensate for another thing by balancing it out, like strong arms making up for short legs.
exercise: «The airline compensated the family for their lost bags.» What does compensated mean here? | *Was given something to make up for the loss | Lost the bags again | Packed the bags very tightly | Chose new bags for fun
exercise: «Dad worked extra hours, so he was compensated with a day off.» What does compensated suggest? | He was sent home sick | *He was given something back for his extra work | He was asked to work even longer | He was spoiled and got no work
exercise: «The body compensated for the cold by shivering to make heat.» What does compensated for mean? | *Made up for the cold | Ignored | Forgot about | Made the cold worse
test: The school compensated the class for the cancelled trip with a film afternoon. What does compensated mean? | *Gave something back to make up for the loss | Cancelled the film | Made the class go home early | Forgot the trip
test: «Her strong arms compensated for her short legs in the race.» Which meaning fits best? | *Her strong arms made up for her short legs | She was made to run slower | She hurt her arms | Her legs grew longer
exam: «After the flood, the family was compensated for the ruined furniture.» What does compensated mean? | *Was given money to make up for the loss | Was moved to a new town | Was told to clean up the mess | Was flooded again
